Bookmarks
description: the push - & gives this node another real path
- >
  `&path` **pushes**: "I *also* live there". The `&` sigil is the **push** operator, and together
  with its path it forms a **bookmark** (generalizing YAML's *anchor* - the historical term, used
  here only as this synonym). A bookmark's name is a full pointer path - same ladder, same
  metacharacters, same escaping - and declaring `&: P: k` on a node means the container at `: P`
  gains the entry `k`: a ref edge to this node, exactly what a forward `k: *me` authored there
  would produce; `normalize` folds the two authorings of one edge together. The authored position
  stays the containment spine and the node's identity path.
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  humans:
    - age: 30
      pet: &: supercat    # ALSO the document-root key "supercat"
        species: cat
    - age: 10
      pet: *: supercat    # a plain path - no bookmark namespace
- >
  **Bookmarks are real keys, not a namespace** - `*name` is pure path lookup; there is no
  precedence rule and no local-versus-global ambiguity. **Bookmarks are not entries**: they never
  count toward a node's kind - a scalar with bookmarks is still a scalar, a blob still a blob; no
  tag is needed to bookmark a scalar. A bookmark attaches to a node; a pointer entry (`k: *p`)
  cannot carry one.
- >
  **Multiplicity and placement.** A node may declare any number of bookmarks: on the value's line
  (quoted when colon-styled - `path: &': another: path' 12`), or - the canonical style - on their
  own lines after the value, where the token runs to end of line unquoted. A whole-document scalar
  is tagged in two bare lines:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  30
  &:: tags: field: mathematics: numbers: whole: -
- >
  **Ordinal bookmarks.** A trailing `-` segment makes the membership keyless: the container gains
  this node as a positional member. No position may be claimed - `&: path: 3` is rejected (a
  bare-integer tail is a position); order is the container's own data
  ([order is data](::language:principles:order-is-data)) - and membership is **additive**: each
  trailing `-` appends one element, lists may repeat - except into a `!!set`, where duplicates
  collapse by target. A `-` anywhere but the trailing position is **reserved**. (The former
  bracket spelling `&path[]` was removed and no longer parses.) Bookmark-created members project
  after the container's own entries, lexicographically by member path. Bookmark paths must be
  **unambiguous**: wildcards and matchers are rejected by the arity rule, position claims by this
  one. A keyed bookmark must end in a nonempty *string* key - it may not create the null key
  either (`&: p: ~` is rejected; the null key is authored in place,
  [null keys](::language:vs-yaml:similarities:null-keys)); the literal-tilde key is fine, quoted
  (`&: p: '~'`).
- >
  **Collisions.** A bookmark-created entry may meet an authored one at the same path - valid
  exactly when the two denote the same thing: the same target node, or structurally equal values.
  Unequal declarations are a **reported conflict**, surfaced like dangling references, never
  silently dropped. In-document bookmarks are checked at parse time; cross-document bookmarks
  (project and world scopes) are realized and checked at index time.
- >
  Relocation needs no special form - point a new place at the existing node with `*`
  (`acting_boss: *: pets: 0`).
